    },
    "body": "Generally this looks good, and I think it is well motivated. I've done what I'll call a \"pseudo editorial review pass\" and by my eyes this has no editorial issues.\r\n\r\nSome meta commentary that's perhaps worth pointing out: `details` elements toggling, and `dialog.show()`/`showModal()`, all dispatch toggle events where the `source` will be `null`. I think that's a little odd, and maybe worth discussing, but I don't see it as problematic to change in a follow-up, or possibly never. For example it might be nice to later add `{source}` as an argument to `show()`/`showModal()`.",
